{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\nSurfaced while fixing `anatomical-arbored-oyster` (e3e0-2e7c-b280-4b4a). Once that fix removed the `FileNotFoundError` collection error (macOS leg) and the `license-files` build `TypeError` (floor leg), the `Test Suite (mirror)` legs run to completion and reveal a large, **pre-existing** failure class that was previously masked.\n\nDominant macOS-leg error (~90 failures across `test_provider_parity`, `test_transport_retry`, `test_llm_fallback_chain`, `test_llm_provider_factory`, `test_llm_timeouts`, `test_web_tool_gating`, `test_llm_config_gate_root`, ...):\n\n```\nError: Invalid `http_client` argument; Expected an instance of `httpx2.AsyncClient` but got <class 'httpx.AsyncClient'>\n```\n\n## Root cause\n\n`pyproject.toml` declares `pydantic-ai-slim[anthropic,retries,duckduckgo]>=1.107,<2` but places **no upper bound on the `anthropic` SDK itself**. The mirror sweep installs UNLOCKED:\n- `sweep (macos, full suite)`: `uv pip install '.[dev,reviewbot,ui]'` (non-editable)\n- `sweep (declared lower-bound resolution)`: `uv pip install --resolution lowest-direct '.[dev,agents]'`\n\nBoth resolve `anthropic==1.2.0`, whose client vendors `httpx2` and **rejects** a stdlib `httpx.AsyncClient`. rebar's provider seam (`src/rebar/llm/anthropic_model.py:_build_retrying_anthropic_provider` -> `anthropic/_client.py:__init__`) passes an `httpx.AsyncClient`, so construction raises `TypeError` and cascades into every Anthropic-touching test. The Verified merge gate is green because `uv.lock` pins an older, compatible anthropic (0.121.0); only the unlocked sweep legs float to 1.2.0.\n\n**httpx2 boundary (verified against PyPI metadata):** the switch to the vendored `httpx2` client happened at anthropic **1.0.0**, not 1.2.0 — anthropic `1.0.0`, `1.1.0`, and `1.2.0` all declare `httpx2<3,>=2.0.0`, while every `0.x` release through `0.125.0` declares stdlib `httpx<1,>=0.25.0`. So the ceiling that excludes the httpx2 line is `<1`, i.e. strictly below `1.0.0`.\n\n## Fix (option (a) — operator-approved, Decision 6): bound `anthropic` in pyproject\n\nAdd a DIRECT, bounded `anthropic` dependency to the `[agents]` extra: `anthropic>=0.121.0,<1`.\n\n- **Ceiling `<1`** excludes the first httpx2-vendoring release (1.0.0) and everything above it, so no sweep resolution can float the SDK onto the httpx2 client the provider seam rejects.\n- **Floor `>=0.121.0`** matches what `uv.lock` resolves and satisfies `pydantic-ai-slim[anthropic]`'s own `anthropic>=0.108.0` requirement. The floor is REQUIRED, not cosmetic: the `sweep (declared lower-bound resolution)` leg uses `--resolution lowest-direct`, and once `anthropic` is a *direct* constraint that leg pins it to the floor. A ceiling-only bound would let that leg drop to an ancient, incompatible anthropic and merely move the failure; `>=0.121.0` lands it on the same verified SDK as the lockfile.\n\nThis is the portable, minimal fix (a declared dependency constraint + a pure-parse packaging unit test — no CI-provider-specific machinery), entirely outside epic `financial-stoneware-brant` (eb64) scope, and it makes the declared bound honest about a known incompatibility `uv.lock` currently masks.\n\n## Scope\n- `pyproject.toml` — add `anthropic>=0.121.0,<1` to `[project.optional-dependencies].agents`.\n- `tests/unit/test_packaging_dependencies.py` — RED oracle asserting the declared `anthropic` bound admits the locked 0.121.0 and excludes the httpx2 releases (1.0.0, 1.2.0).\n\n**Out of scope (do NOT touch):** `src/rebar/llm/` (incl. `anthropic_model.py`), the reconciler, CLI/commands, store, workflows, ADRs — all eb64 territory. Option (b) (adapt the provider seam to the httpx2 `http_client` contract) is split to follow-up `2bd6-ff87-d48c-4a65`, BLOCKED on eb64/254e.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] `pyproject.toml`'s `[agents]` extra declares a DIRECT `anthropic` dependency with BOTH a floor and a ceiling; the ceiling excludes the httpx2-vendoring line (`<1`).\n- [ ] A packaging unit test asserts the declared `anthropic` specifier admits `0.121.0` (locked, stdlib-httpx) and rejects `1.0.0` and `1.2.0` (httpx2); it fails RED if the ceiling is removed.\n- [ ] A fresh resolution of `.[agents]` — both highest-version AND `--resolution lowest-direct` — resolves `anthropic` to a `0.x` (stdlib-httpx) release, so the Anthropic provider constructs without the `Invalid http_client ... httpx2.AsyncClient` `TypeError`.\n- [ ] The fix is portable across CI providers / no CI (a declared dependency constraint + a pure pyproject-parse test; no CI-system-specific trigger).\n\n## Evidence\n- Mirror run 33299427686 (dispatched on `main` post-fix): `sweep (macos, full suite)` job 99224621948, `sweep (declared lower-bound resolution)` job 99224621821. `anthropic==1.2.0` shown installing in the macOS leg; error string above aggregated 90x.\n- Local RED repro (this session): `uv pip compile` of `.[agents]` at both highest and `lowest-direct` resolutions selects `anthropic==1.2.0` + `httpx2==2.12.0`; constructing `AsyncAnthropic(http_client=httpx.AsyncClient())` under anthropic 1.2.0 raises the exact `TypeError`; under `anthropic==0.121.0` it constructs cleanly."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788112044202304381,"uuid":"f97b92bd-658a-47d9-acc9-c6f5e12170d6"}